der Partial Derivatives"}] :question/problem "Find $\dfrac {\partial^2 f }{\partial x\partial y}$ given that $\dfrac {\partial f}{\partial y} =  \dfrac {2y} {x + y^2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\dfrac {\partial^2 f }{\partial x\partial y},$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\dfrac {\partial f}{\partial y}$ with respect to $x\mathbin{:}$

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(\frac{∂f}{∂y}) \\  & =\frac{∂}{∂x}(\frac{2y}{x+{y}^{2}}) \\  & =2y\cdot \frac{∂}{∂x}({(x+{y}^{2})}^{-1}) \\  & =-2y(x+{y}^{2})^{-2}\cdot 1 \\  & =-\frac{2y}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}}\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186050902} {:db/id 17592186124935 :question/id #uuid "a2fb72a1-759b-5104-b498-90f4bee3c6d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-35947"} {:db/id 17592186125185 :question/id #uuid "4b485a7d-6344-562d-8806-b57dc4f057da" :question/math-academy-id "q-65057"} {:db/id 17592186235546 :question/id #uuid "c850286e-676c-54c4-ab09-fb3da5e5b980" :question/math-academy-id "q-168866"} {:db/id 17592186268915 :question/id #uuid "9ff84a14-2b18-5ea3-8551-3c53774a8d4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-132764"} {:db/id 17592186268916 :question/id #uuid "12894c28-d9fc-5b1a-9ce3-909e531bc682" :question/math-academy-id "q-132800"} {:db/id 17592186335782 :question/id #uuid "435d066b-0de3-5e62-8775-943aacab7cbf" :question/math-academy-id "q-65058"} {:db/id 17592186335784 :question/id #uuid "a96b5224-3589-5ee6-9e32-9c7fe293ceb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-65060"} {:db/id 17592186348377 :question/id #uuid "fa43a83f-a97a-54b7-8060-e07ac7e5d1a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-80396"} {:db/id 17592186382138 :question/id #uuid "ca9f5fb8-f9bc-5351-b359-d64e2aa35cc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-65065" :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186124440 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ea31275-77bd-59c7-8e1d-96e2e4b252a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Mixed Second-Order Partial Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86e47b3c-f8f9-5e18-9d28-6f36b2c27a42" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{{x}^{3}-{y}^{3}}{{x}^{3}+{y}^{3}}" :db/id 17592186382140} {:answer/id #uuid "6188f36a-ac69-5d7a-b9fc-397b48fca9ee" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{{x}^{3}}{{({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})}^{2}}" :db/id 17592186382141} {:answer/id #uuid "291c128e-6369-5cd6-aadd-033a32d1485e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{y({x}^{3}-{y}^{3})}{{({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})}^{2}}" :db/id 17592186382142} {:answer/id #uuid "ed41aa2c-c8b0-5b09-a441-f7cad2ab71a6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{3y(2{x}^{3}-{y}^{3})}{{({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})}^{2}}" :db/id 17592186382143} {:answer/id #uuid "dcba6b3f-e253-5f01-8e9a-cad9140c3ae4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{-{y}^{3}}{{x}^{3}+{y}^{3}}" :db/id 17592186382144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed41aa2c-c8b0-5b09-a441-f7cad2ab71a6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{3y(2{x}^{3}-{y}^{3})}{{({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})}^{2}}" :db/id 17592186382143} :answer-field/id #uuid "b09ec52c-6763-5e59-8f36-60c753f9258b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186382139}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}$ given that $\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\frac{3{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}+{y}^{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ with respect to $y:$

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(\frac{∂f}{∂y}) \\  & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(\frac{3{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}+{y}^{3}}) \\  & =\frac{6y({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})-3{y}^{2}(3{y}^{2})}{{({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})}^{2}} \\  & =\frac{6y{x}^{3}+6{y}^{4}-9{y}^{4}}{{({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})}^{2}} \\  & =\frac{6y{x}^{3}-3{y}^{4}}{{({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})}^{2}} \\  & =\frac{3y(2{x}^{3}-{y}^{3})}{{({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})}^{2}}\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186382358 :question/id #uuid "e96e8c39-27d3-5b9a-9e75-bf048a578366" :question/math-academy-id "q-80395"} {:db/id 17592186382365 :question/id #uuid "27410c7b-bcd3-51b0-ad2f-12407bb83068" :question/math-academy-id "q-80398" :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186124440 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ea31275-77bd-59c7-8e1d-96e2e4b252a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Mixed Second-Order Partial Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ab3f9a2-c043-533c-ad7b-13b9b79758f7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy(y+2){e}^{{x}^{2}+2y}" :db/id 17592186382367} {:answer/id #uuid "3110f91f-c3d2-5e2b-91df-c4a5c455454f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x+y){e}^{{x}^{2}+2y}" :db/id 17592186382368} {:answer/id #uuid "54f651dc-5268-59e5-9c63-07f1939806db" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y(y+1){e}^{{x}^{2}+2y}" :db/id 17592186382369} {:answer/id #uuid "c910c31d-50d6-5437-9055-00c5404b90a8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y{e}^{{x}^{2}+2y}" :db/id 17592186382370} {:answer/id #uuid "7cf17aee-0b17-5afe-b71a-fd27bd564088" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x{y}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}+2y}" :db/id 17592186382371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54f651dc-5268-59e5-9c63-07f1939806db" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y(y+1){e}^{{x}^{2}+2y}" :db/id 17592186382369} :answer-field/id #uuid "73748794-1a7d-52b6-9351-18509da54bfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186382366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x}$ given that $\frac{∂f}{∂x}={y}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}+2y}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $y:$

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\frac{∂}{∂y}(\frac{∂f}{∂x}) \\  & =\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}+2y}) \\  & =2y{e}^{{x}^{2}+2y}+2{y}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}+2y} \\  & =2y(y+1){e}^{{x}^{2}+2y}\end{aligned}
